    {
      "v": 3,
      "zh": "因为往日随从外邦人的心意行邪淫、恶欲、醉酒、荒宴、群饮，并可恶拜偶像的事，时候已经够了。",
      "en": "For the time that has passed was sufficient for you to do what the non-Christians[NOTE:1] desire.[NOTE:2] You lived then[NOTE:3] in debauchery, evil desires, drunkenness, carousing, drinking bouts,[NOTE:4] and wanton idolatries.[NOTE:5]",
      "notes": [
        "Grk “the Gentiles,” used here of those who are not God’s people.",
        "Grk “to accomplish the desire of the Gentiles.”",
        "Grk “having gone along,” referring to the readers’ behavior in time past.",
        "According to BDAG 857 s.v. πότος the term refers to a social gathering at which wine is served, hence “drinking parties” (cf. TEV, NASB). However, the collocation with the other terms in v. 4 suggests something less sophisticated and more along the lines of wild and frenzied drinking bouts.",
        "The Greek words here all occur in the plural to describe their common practice in the past."
